Third-party software

packages/floorplan depends on polygon-clipping 0.15.7 (https://github.com/mfogel/polygon-clipping),
under the MIT License, Copyright (c) 2018 Mike Fogel and Copyright (c) 2016 Alexander Milevski.
Grid uses it to join wall footprints into the spaces they enclose
(packages/floorplan/src/geometry/spaces.ts). It is a dependency, not copied code. The bundled
`grid` command includes it, and with it its two dependencies:

- splaytree (https://github.com/w8r/splay-tree), under the MIT License,
  Copyright (c) 2019 Alexander Milevski;
- robust-predicates (https://github.com/mourner/robust-predicates), by Vladimir Agafonkin,
  released into the public domain under the Unlicense.

Their full licence texts are in their packages.

The ongrid package draws its PNG pictures with @napi-rs/canvas 1.1.0
(https://github.com/Brooooooklyn/canvas), under the MIT License, Copyright (c) 2020 its author,
as its LICENSE file states. It is a dependency, not copied code: the npm package lists it as
optional and grid.mjs leaves it out (packages/cli/build.mjs), and the bundle for Claude's
desktop app (.mcpb) carries it unchanged, with its LICENSE, under server/node_modules/. Its
ready-built binary holds Skia and other libraries, each under its own licence, which the
binary's package lists in its sbom.cdx.json.

